From: Cris <tuputamadre7015@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: offload IPv6 flows of WiFi clients through WHNAT

Lab port of kernel-whnat-ipv6 70591a0a1 to the Plan C kernel: offer
routed IPv6 TCP/UDP unicast frames (not link-local) to the PPE and let
IPv6 5T routes target a vif. Off by default in this lab image, so a boot
is exactly Plan C; echo 1 > /sys/module/airoha_eth/parameters/whnat_ipv6
turns it on.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -3489,10 +3489,12 @@
 	if (wifi_idx >= 0) {
 		/*
 		 * Vendor WHNAT recipe: the CPU as PSE port, without QoS, and
-		 * the vif index in an 802.1Q tag. Only IPv4 has been tested.
+		 * the vif index in an 802.1Q tag. IPv6 5T routes take the
+		 * same tag; whnat_ipv6 can keep them on the CPU.
 		 */
 		if (vlan_valid ||
-		    airoha_foe_v1_packet_type(entry) == PPE_PKT_TYPE_IPV6_ROUTE_5T)
+		    (airoha_foe_v1_packet_type(entry) == PPE_PKT_TYPE_IPV6_ROUTE_5T &&
+		     !airoha_whnat_ipv6()))
 			return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 
 		airoha_foe_v1_entry_set_pse_port(entry, FE_PSE_PORT_CDM1);
